---
import SomiBase from '../../layouts/SomiBase.astro'
import DocHeader from '../../components/somi/DocHeader.astro'
import { COMPANY, CONTACT, LEGAL_UPDATED, SITE, p } from '../../somi/config.js'
---

<SomiBase
  title="Privacy Policy"
  variant="document"
  description="How SoMi collects, uses, stores and deletes your information."
>
  <DocHeader
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    lede="What SoMi collects, why, who else can see it, and how to get rid of all of it."
    updated={LEGAL_UPDATED}
  />

  <article class="prose-somi mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-28 pt-4 sm:px-8">
    <p>
      This policy explains how {COMPANY.name} (“we”, “us”) handles information in
      the SoMi iPhone app and on {SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}. It applies
      to the app and this website, and to nothing else.
    </p>

    <p>
      The short version: SoMi stores the account information needed to sign you
      in and the check-ins, notes, tags and practice history you choose to save.
      Limited product analytics and crash diagnostics help us improve the app.
      <strong
        >SoMi has no ads or advertising trackers, and we do not sell your data.</strong
      > You can permanently delete your account and practice history from the app.
    </p>

    <h2 id="what-we-collect">1. What we collect</h2>

    <h3>Account information</h3>
    <p>
      When you create an account we store an account identifier and either the
      email address you registered with, or the identifier Apple provides when
      you use <strong>Sign in with Apple</strong>. If you choose Apple’s
      <em>Hide My Email</em> option, we only ever receive Apple’s relay address —
      not your real one.
    </p>
    <p>
      Passwords for email accounts are handled by our authentication provider
      and stored only as salted hashes. We never see or store your password in
      readable form.
    </p>

    <h3>Practice information you enter</h3>
    <p>
      This is the data SoMi exists to hold. It is stored against your account so
      that the app can show you your own history:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Check-ins.</strong> The energy and safety values you set on the
        state map, recorded as two numbers from 0 to 100, before and after a
        session.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Somatic tags.</strong> Any experience tags you select at
        check-out, such as sighing, shaking, warmth or laughter.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Journal notes.</strong> Free text you choose to write. This is
        optional and always initiated by you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Session records.</strong> Which exercises played, in what order,
        for how many seconds, and when the session happened. These drive your
        calendar, minutes and completion stats. Your check-in history drives
        your attendance streak; completed Daily Flows remain recorded separately.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Usage and diagnostic information</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Product analytics.</strong> Usage events are linked to an account
        identifier and analyzed to understand patterns such as completion and
        drop-off. <strong
          >They do not contain your email, journal text or actual tags.</strong
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Crash and error reports.</strong> These may include the device
        model, operating system version, app version and account information
        needed to investigate the problem. Sensitive fields such as passwords,
        tokens and journal entries are stripped before a report is sent.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        SoMi does not request access to your device’s GPS location. Service
        providers may process an IP address when delivering the app and its services.
      </li>
      <li>No contacts, photos, calendar or health-app data. SoMi does not read from Apple Health.</li>
      <li>
        No microphone or camera access. The app plays audio and video; it does
        not record any.
      </li>
      <li>No advertising identifiers, and no third-party advertising SDKs.</li>
      <li>No payment information. SoMi is free and has no in-app purchases.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="how-we-use-it">2. How we use it</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Information</th><th>Why we have it</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Account identifier and email</td>
          <td>To sign you in and keep your practice history attached to you</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Check-ins, tags and journal notes</td>
          <td>
            To show you your own history and to shape the flow the app composes
            for you; check-ins also calculate your attendance streak
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Session records</td>
          <td>To show your calendar, minutes, completed Daily Flows and completion stats</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Analytics events</td>
          <td>
            To understand completion and drop-off patterns so we can improve the app
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Crash reports</td>
          <td>To find and fix bugs</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
      We do not use your information to build advertising profiles, and we do not
      run automated decision-making that produces legal or similarly significant
      effects.
    </p>

    <h2 id="legal-bases">3. Legal bases (UK and EEA users)</h2>
    <p>
      Where the UK GDPR or EU GDPR applies, we rely on: <strong>contract</strong>
      for account and practice data, because without it the app cannot function;
      and <strong>legitimate interests</strong> for analytics and crash reporting,
      to keep the app working and improve it. You can object to processing based
      on legitimate interests at any time by writing to {CONTACT.privacy}.
    </p>

    <h2 id="who-else">4. Who else processes your data</h2>
    <p>
      We use service providers for hosting, authentication, data storage, product
      analytics, crash reporting, app distribution and Sign in with Apple. They
      process information for us to operate and improve SoMi and are not permitted
      to use it for their own purposes.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may also disclose information if we are legally required to, or to
      protect the rights and safety of our users or ourselves.
    </p>

    <h2 id="transfers">5. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      We are based in {COMPANY.city}, {COMPANY.state}, and our providers process
      data in the United States. If you use SoMi from outside the United States,
      your information will be transferred there. Where required, our providers
      rely on Standard Contractual Clauses or equivalent safeguards for these
      transfers.
    </p>

    <h2 id="retention">6. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Account and practice data is kept for as long as your account exists,
      because its whole purpose is to be your history. When you delete your
      account we delete it — see the next section. Analytics and crash reports
      are kept by our service providers on rolling retention windows. You can
      contact us if you want those records included in a deletion request.
    </p>

    <h2 id="your-rights">7. Your rights and your controls</h2>
    <p>You can, at any time:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Delete your account and practice history</strong> from inside the
        app, in two taps from the Profile tab. This is a permanent deletion, not
        a deactivation. Step-by-step instructions are on our
        <a href={p('/account-deletion')}>account deletion page</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Ask for a copy of your data</strong>, or ask us to correct
        something, by emailing {CONTACT.privacy}.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Object to or restrict</strong> analytics processing by emailing
        us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Withdraw consent</strong> where we relied on it, without
        affecting processing that already happened.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We answer requests within 30 days. If you are in the UK or EEA you also
      have the right to complain to your local data protection authority. If you
      are a California resident, you have the rights described in the CCPA/CPRA
      to know, delete, and correct your personal information, and not to be
      discriminated against for exercising them. <strong
        >We do not sell or share personal information as those terms are defined
        under California law.</strong
      >
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">8. Children</h2>
    <p>
      SoMi’s practices may be used by people of all ages. Account creation is for
      people age 13 and older, or older where local law requires a higher minimum
      age. Parents and guardians may guide younger children through SoMi using
      the adult’s own account. If you are a parent or legal guardian and believe
      a child under 13, or under a higher applicable age where they live, has
      given us personal information, write to {CONTACT.privacy} and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="security">9. Security</h2>
    <p>
      Data is encrypted in transit. Access to your practice records is enforced
      at the database level, so one account cannot read another’s rows. No system
      is perfectly secure, but we keep the amount of data we hold deliberately
      small, which is the most reliable protection there is.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">10. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we change this policy we will update the date at the top of this page.
      For material changes we will also notify you in the app before the change
      takes effect.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">11. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {COMPANY.name}<br />
      {COMPANY.addressLine}<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.privacy}`}>{CONTACT.privacy}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</SomiBase>
